aded with 16 patients, while **Dr. Priya Nair** in the same department has only 3 patients.\n- Click **10. Reassignment** in the sidebar.\n- You will see an active proposal:\n  - *Problem:* Doctor workload imbalance.\n  - *Action:* Reassign 6 normal-priority patients from Dr. Rajesh Sharma to Dr. Priya Nair.\n  - *Benefit:* Saves ~55 minutes of queue time for Room 101.\n- Click **APPROVE REASSIGNMENT**.\n- Go back to **3. Patient Queue** or **5. Doctor Workload**: You will see that 6 patients were moved to Dr. Priya Nair, and both queues recalculated their waiting times.\n\n#### 5. Test Bed Occupancy & 4-Hour Hourly Forecast (`Section 7`)\n- Click **7. Bed Occupancy** in the sidebar.\n- Look at the **Cardiology Ward**: It shows high occupancy (92%) with a red alert: *\"Cardiology may experience bed capacity shortage within the next three hours.\"*\n- View the **+1h, +2h, +3h, +4h** forecast columns and the forecast trend chart.\n- Click **Simulate Admission (+1 Bed)** or **Simulate Discharge (-1 Bed)** at the top right to see the occupancy percentages and charts update in real time.\n\n#### 6. Test Disease Outbreak & Inventory Linkage (`Section 8 & 9`)\n- Click **8. Disease Trends** in the sidebar.\n- Review the 14-day history chart showing an escalating Dengue trend and tomorrow's projected cases.\n- Click the button **Simulate Dengue Spike (+15)** at the top right.\n- Now switch to **9. Inventory**:\n  - Notice that **Dengue NS1 Antigen Rapid Test Kits** and **IV Normal Saline** immediately trigger a **CRITICAL Shortage Alert** because of the disease surge.\n  - Click **Restock** next to the item, enter `150`, and watch the stock level recover to Normal (Green).\n\n#### 7. Test the Hackathon Simulation Lab (`Section 12`)\n- Click **12. Simulation Lab** in the sidebar.\n- Here you can test everything simultaneously:\n  - Inject a burst of **+10 Normal Patients** or **+3 Emergency Patients**.\n  - Toggle a doctor's status to **On Break**.\n  - If you ever want to restart from the beginning, click **Reset Simulation to Baseline**.\n\n#### 8. Inspect the Machine Learning Evaluation (`Section 13`)\n- Click **13. ML Performance** in the sidebar.\n- View the real validation metrics computed on the test split:\n  - **Random Forest:** $R^2 \\approx 0.996$, $\\text{MAE} \\approx 10.0\\text{ mins}$, $\\text{RMSE} \\approx 13.7\\text{ mins}$.\n  - **Linear Regression Baseline:** $R^2 \\approx 0.860$, $\\text{MAE} \\approx 59.7\\text{ mins}$.\n  - View the **Feature Importance** chart explaining which factors influence wait times the most (`patients_ahead`, `avg_consult_duration`, `priority_code`, etc.).\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: How to Run It in Any Terminal (For Later)\n\nIf you reboot your computer or want to launch it from a new terminal window:\n\n```powershell\ncd \"C:\\Users\\KRUTIKA SHIVANAND\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\queue-oracle\"\npython app.py\n```\nThen simply open `http://127.0.0.1:5000` in your browser."}
